sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/wolfram2002-ch02-03> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "As a general phenomenon, a system with simple underlying rules started from simple initial conditions can nevertheless show highly complex behavior.";
    dc:type "general-principle";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Simple rules with simple initial conditions can yield highly complex behavior";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Stephen Wolfram, A New Kind of Science (Champaign, IL: Wolfram Media, 2002), Chapter 2, “The Crucial Experiment”; section “How Do Simple Programs Behave?” (from p. 23), p. 28. Scope: simple programs and other systems with simple rules and simple initial conditions"
}
